WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.890
how do you balance extreme ownership
with holding others accountable for

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:11.400
their actions and avoiding them using
you so this is actually a question that

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:17.820
I end up responding to on a fairly
regular basis and there's really a

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:23.490
couple different angles here that are
going on the one of the the points here

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:29.369
is the balance of extreme ownership
versus holding others accountable and

00:00:29.369 --> 00:00:33.300
what that really means and or what
another way of looking at that is it's

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:40.079
really extreme ownership versus
decentralized command so decentralized

00:00:40.079 --> 00:00:46.860
command is it's one of the laws of
combat that life and I write about in

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:51.390
the book decentralized command and what
that means is everybody leads that means

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:57.149
everybody's a leader and that's what you
want and that is a that is a the

00:00:57.149 --> 00:01:01.980
complete opposite of extreme ownership
so extreme ownership I'm that I own

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:05.189
everything
decentralized command is I'm gonna let

00:01:05.189 --> 00:01:10.590
everyone else lead so there's a real a
real contradiction a real dichotomy

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:17.729
there so what you have to do is balance
it you have to balance it's the only way

00:01:17.729 --> 00:01:25.400
to to sort of rectify or ret or
reconcile those two opposing forces

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:30.119
because you do but you do have to have
extreme ownership of everything that is

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:33.329
true and at the same time you have to
have decentralized commander because you

00:01:33.329 --> 00:01:37.770
can't be everywhere at once and you have
to let your frontline leaders lead so

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:44.790
you have to balance them so that's one
part of it is that you should if you

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:50.130
feel yourself for instance if you feel
like you can't get everything done and

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:56.340
you're losing control or you're you're
not able to execute everything because

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:00.270
there's too much on your plate it means
that you're not delegating enough it

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:03.170
means that you're not your frontline
troopers aren't stepping up and leading

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:09.989
now so you've gone too far in one
direction now if you're leaders or if

00:02:09.989 --> 00:02:13.680
all of a sudden you're having to tell
your leaders like eh

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:15.989
you need to get this done hey what are
you doing why don't you take an

00:02:15.989 --> 00:02:19.049
initiative then that means you've gone
too far in the other direction so you

00:02:19.049 --> 00:02:23.909
have to find the good balance and that's
the that's the goal and again and I'll

00:02:23.909 --> 00:02:27.420
say it over and over again that's what
makes leadership hard leadership the

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:30.780
hardest thing about leadership is that
there's opposing forces that you have to

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:34.319
balance and if you could just pick the
extreme and go with it and that made you

00:02:34.319 --> 00:02:38.400
a good leader anyone could do it but
it's not it's it's the balance that

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:44.879
makes you a good leader it's the balance
that's challenging so now the other word

00:02:44.879 --> 00:02:53.129
so that's part of the question the other
word is accountability in holding people

00:02:53.129 --> 00:02:59.849
accountable for their actions now this
is where I'm gonna throw something out

00:02:59.849 --> 00:03:05.359
that people are not going to expect me
to say because people always talk about

00:03:05.359 --> 00:03:11.010
accountability and I hear that all the
time in businesses and they say yeah we

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:16.010
really need accountability
accountability accountability and here's

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:24.480
the issue I have with that you don't
want to have to rely on accountability

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:31.139
accountability is actually a crutch
it's a tool and I'm not saying you never

00:03:31.139 --> 00:03:34.829
use it because sometimes you do have to
use it you have to implement it if

00:03:34.829 --> 00:03:37.290
people aren't doing what they're
supposed to do you have to hold them

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:44.489
accountable but I will tell you this
what you what you don't want it's people

00:03:44.489 --> 00:03:49.949
that are doing their job only because
you're holding them accountable that's

00:03:49.949 --> 00:03:55.650
not what you want you want people that
take initiative and ownership of their

00:03:55.650 --> 00:04:00.000
job and they do it not because you want
them to or because you're going to

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:06.660
inspect them they do it because they own
it they take extreme ownership of it

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:14.849
that's what you want so if you were to
ask people that work for me if I held

00:04:14.849 --> 00:04:18.630
them accountable and they would be like
mmm not really

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:25.349
I mean for instance weapons inspections
so you know I'm in charge of a platoon

00:04:25.349 --> 00:04:29.659
or I'm in charge of a task unit
and there's you know a couple hundred

00:04:29.659 --> 00:04:35.000
weapons or whatever a bunch of weapons
and if you don't take care of those

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:39.889
weapons and people don't maintain them
and clean them and lubricate them

00:04:39.889 --> 00:04:44.330
properly they can rust very easily
mm-hmm and so we know one of the things

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:48.979
that you may have to do is do weapons
and inspections to make sure that my

00:04:48.979 --> 00:04:58.580
guys are cleaning their weapons and I
can tell you I rarely if ever conducted

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:06.319
actual weapons inspections the reason my
guys my guys did it

00:05:06.319 --> 00:05:13.250
my guys owned it my guys wanted to be
the best they wanted to always have the

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:19.629
best possible reputation and so I'd have
to go around inspecting their weapons

00:05:19.629 --> 00:05:25.129
because I knew that they were gonna do
it I knew that that my guys who were on

00:05:25.129 --> 00:05:30.979
board who understood why we were doing
what we were doing mm-hmm who understood

00:05:30.979 --> 00:05:35.680
that we wanted to be the best and who
were on board with trying to be the best

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:41.210
said you know what you know we are gonna
make sure these weapons are the best

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:47.479
possible and I learned this when I was
in my second platoon my boss was an

00:05:47.479 --> 00:05:51.830
awesome guy and this is a guy that I've
talked about before he was a huge

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:57.919
influence on me he was a prior enlisted
SEAL who became an officer he was a

00:05:57.919 --> 00:06:04.490
combat veteran from the warned Renata
and he was a very humble guy and he's

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:07.669
actually the guy that inspired me to
become an officer because I said to

00:06:07.669 --> 00:06:12.919
myself well this guy's this guy made our
lives so good maybe I could do that for

00:06:12.919 --> 00:06:19.909
16 guys in a platoon someday but what I
realized about him is he never held us

00:06:19.909 --> 00:06:27.289
accountable for anything but at the same
time he infused accountability on us

00:06:27.289 --> 00:06:31.639
because what we wanted more than
anything else was to do a good job for

00:06:31.639 --> 00:06:37.540
him and for the platoon that's that's
how you get true

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:43.720
and teams aligned not by holding them
accountable when the imposed

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:49.420
accountability but where they are
inspired themselves to hold themselves

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:56.620
accountable and you had a coaching call
with a team the other day that was they

00:06:56.620 --> 00:07:00.940
were saying hey you know we really we
really we would like to have you you

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:04.060
know
coach us because we're lacking in these

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:08.080
areas and we really need we know what to
do but we really need someone to hold us

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:17.650
accountable to do it hmm and I was like
lesson I charge a lot of money and you

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:23.710
guys would be stupid to give it to me
you guys just simply lack the discipline

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:28.990
to work for the team and make it happen
and I threw this example I said you know

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:34.060
if you were competing against another
team and what I did was I moved into

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:36.550
your house and I woke you up in the
morning and I held you accountable for

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:40.300
what you were supposed to do and I made
you do it so we put the ultimate in

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:47.050
accountability on top of them I said who
would do better you guys with me waking

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:51.070
you up in the morning and beating you
until you accomplished what you were

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:55.240
supposed to do I held you to the up the
highest standard of accountability or a

00:07:55.240 --> 00:08:03.220
team that was hungry themselves that was
gonna go the extra mile that was gonna

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:07.210
do more work that was gonna stay up
later that was gonna get up earlier not

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:11.230
because somebody was holding them
accountable but because they had the

00:08:11.230 --> 00:08:18.190
desire for victory who's gonna win that
contest and the answer is very simple

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:25.870
those with the innate and intrinsic
desire to win will win over those that

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:31.110
have imposed discipline and
accountability put on top of them now

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:34.150
because there's a dichotomy to
everything and because there's a balance

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:38.380
to everything there are times where in a
leadership position you do need to

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:43.150
inspect and make sure that you hold
people accountable and an example I have

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:49.330
that is we had when we got to Ramadi we
had our radios and generally the radio

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:52.019
men
knew how to program the radios and and

00:08:52.019 --> 00:08:55.949
get them synched up so they could talk
to other radios and all that and I told

00:08:55.949 --> 00:09:00.600
the guys I'm like listen everybody in
the troop needs to know how to program

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:04.500
your radio yourself and if it says oh
okay

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:11.310
and it was so critical that they know
how to program these radios because if

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:13.680
you're out in the field and you get
separated from your unit and all of a

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:17.189
sudden your radio gets zero eyes or it
has a problem and you don't know how to

00:09:17.189 --> 00:09:20.189
fix it yourself what are you gonna do
you can't talk to anybody and you're

00:09:20.189 --> 00:09:22.829
doomed
you're gonna die so because it was that

00:09:22.829 --> 00:09:28.500
critical I actually after the first
briefing I called a couple guys up and I

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:32.759
said give me a radio and I zero eyes
their radios and I said okay reprogram

00:09:32.759 --> 00:09:38.129
it now and a couple of them didn't know
how to do it and I said okay listen up

00:09:38.129 --> 00:09:40.800
guys
no one is going on operation if you

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:44.939
can't reprogram your radio and so the
guys had to sit down and go and figure

00:09:44.939 --> 00:09:48.480
out how to do it so there's times where
you you do have to hold people

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:52.379
accountable and in that situation I knew
that even though I was saying hey it's

00:09:52.379 --> 00:09:55.889
important they didn't realize how
important it was because you know it was

00:09:55.889 --> 00:09:58.350
all you got to know how to work your
gear they kind of took it like that

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:01.800
I knew that guys didn't really
understand the nature of how important

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:06.360
it was to be able to operate and
reprogram your entire radio and sync it

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:10.860
with the army radios and all that I knew
that they didn't quite understand how

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:16.370
important it was and so I had to I had
to hold them accountable but generally

00:10:16.370 --> 00:10:20.819
ninety-eight percent of the stuff I
didn't have to hold people accountable

00:10:20.819 --> 00:10:29.279
I didn't inspect things I expected
things and they delivered yeah and and

00:10:29.279 --> 00:10:35.040
that's that's people will follow your
lead if you take ownership that's how my

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:43.920
guys have always been they've always
seen that and and known what the

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:49.620
expectations were and finally if if
you're sitting there and you keep saying

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:51.899
here so if I gotta hold people
accountable I gotta hold people

00:10:51.899 --> 00:10:59.880
accountable most likely you don't need
to hold them accountable you need to

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:03.980
lead them you
to make them understand why they're

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:08.540
doing what they're doing why it's
important how it impacts the strategic

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:15.680
mission how it impacts the team how it
impacts them that's leadership non

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:20.030
accountability its leadership
accountability is just a tool and it is

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:29.690
a a it's a crude tool compared to real
leadership so use it if you have to but

00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:35.890
try and use leadership instead

